==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*tunglą}}, cognate with Old High German {{m|goh|zungal}} (see there) and Old English {{m|ang|tungol}}. Further etymology unknown; Pokorny reconstructs a PIE root ''*dengh-'' "to shine" just from this Germanic word and a Baltic word for "to seem, to appear" (Lithuanian ''diñga'').

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n}}

# [[moon]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|non|tunglskin}}

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|tungl}}
* Old Swedish: [[tungel]]
** Swedish: {{l|sv|tungel}} (dated and dialectal)

